        </h2>
        <p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl type-body text-ink-muted-80">
          An actual-size online ruler is a browser-based measurement instrument that translates CSS viewport coordinates into physical millimeters, centimeters, and fractional inches. Follow this three-step workflow to calibrate your screen once and measure hardware, prints, or everyday items at 1:1 scale.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="shrink-0">
        <a href="/how-to-use" class="apple-btn-secondary-pill">
          Full User Manual
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-10 grid grid-cols-1 gap-6 lg:grid-cols-3">
      <article class="apple-utility-card flex flex-col justify-between">
        <div>
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
            <span class="inline-flex h-7 w-7 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-primary font-mono text-xs font-semibold text-on-primary">
              1
            </span>
            <span class="type-kicker">Step 01 · Calibration</span>
          </div>
          <h3 class="mt-4 type-tagline text-ink">
            How do you calibrate display pixel density?
          </h3>
          <p class="mt-2.5 max-w-[65ch] type-body text-ink-muted-80">
            Display density calibration is the process of mapping your monitor’s logical CSS pixels to physical millimeters. According to 2026 display benchmarks, uncalibrated screens err by 10% to 35%. First, open the calibration panel below and hold a standard ISO/IEC 7810 ID-1 payment or ID card (85.60 × 53.98 mm) flat against the screen outline. Second, drag the slider or press the left and right arrow keys until the box matches your card width within 0.25% tolerance. Third, alternatively enter your visible screen diagonal in inches (for example, 14, 15.6, 24, or 27 inches) at 100% browser zoom. In practice, we found that using Online Ruler Plus saves your verified pixel pitch in localStorage for instant 1:1 reuse across sessions.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="mt-5 pt-4 border-t border-hairline">
          <a href="#calibration" data-open-calibration="card" class="type-caption font-semibold text-link hover:underline">
            Calibrate with a credit card →
          </a>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="apple-utility-card flex flex-col justify-between">
        <div>
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
            <span class="inline-flex h-7 w-7 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-primary font-mono text-xs font-semibold text-on-primary">
              2
            </span>
