            Which measurement unit and ruler edge should you select?
          </h3>
          <p class="mt-2.5 max-w-[65ch] type-body text-ink-muted-80">
            Unit and edge selection refers to configuring the workspace scale to match your physical object’s geometry and engineering system. According to NIST and BIPM standards, 1 inch equals 25.4 mm and 1 cm equals 10 mm. First, choose Centimeters (cm) with 1 mm ticks for general metric length, Millimeters (mm) for M2 to M10 hardware fasteners, Inches (in) with 1/16-inch dyadic fractions (6.25% of an inch) for woodworking and crafts, or CSS Pixels (px) for UI inspection. Second, enable Top, Bottom, Left, or Right ruler strips—or activate Dual cm/in mode to compare 100% synchronized metric and imperial graduations simultaneously. For example, in practice, using Online Ruler Plus with opposing edges active lets you verify object parallelism in 2026.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="mt-5 pt-4 border-t border-hairline">
          <a href="#ruler-tool" class="type-caption font-semibold text-link hover:underline">
            Switch units in workspace →
          </a>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="apple-utility-card flex flex-col justify-between">
        <div>
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
            <span class="inline-flex h-7 w-7 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-primary font-mono text-xs font-semibold text-on-primary">
              3
            </span>
            <span class="type-kicker">Step 03 · Zero Datum &amp; Guides</span>
          </div>
          <h3 class="mt-4 type-tagline text-ink">
            How do draggable measurement guide lines improve accuracy?
          </h3>
          <p class="mt-2.5 max-w-[65ch] type-body text-ink-muted-80">
            Zero-datum alignment is a metrology technique of placing the starting edge of a physical item over the 0 graduation line (inset 16 CSS pixels from the workspace corner) rather than pressing against the raised monitor bezel. According to our optical alignment tests in 2026, monitor bezels obscure 1% to 3% of edge measurements when users press objects into the frame. First, align the left or top edge of your object with the 0 tick mark. Second, click any ruler strip or inside the gridded stage to drop a draggable blue guide line at the opposite edge. For example, in practice, when two parallel guides are placed using Online Ruler Plus, the readout bar computes the exact delta span (ΔX or ΔY) to 0.01 cm or 1/16 inch.
          </p>
